  "type": "Album + Live",
  "description": "Unplugged is a 1992 live album by the English guitarist Eric Clapton, recorded at Bray Studios in Windsor, England, in front of an audience for the MTV Unplugged TV series. It includes performances of the songs \"Tears in Heaven\" (1992) and \"Layla\" (1970). The album won three Grammy Awards at the 35th Annual Grammy Awards in 1993. It became the best-selling live album of all time, and Clapton's best-selling album, selling 26 million copies worldwide.",
